<!-- Hostile PROPFIND fixture.

     A DAV:multistatus shaped exactly like the recorded Receita Federal body
     (tests/fixtures/files/cnpj_propfind_recorded.xml) but carrying the four entries a
     real share never returns. The share token is the literal SHARE_TOKEN, so the source
     URL this is parsed against is
         https://arquivos.receitafederal.gov.br/index.php/s/SHARE_TOKEN
     and the origin every verdict is measured against is
         (https, arquivos.receitafederal.gov.br, 443).

     Verdicts, in document order:
       1. /public.php/webdav/                          skipped today — resourcetype/collection
       2. /public.php/webdav/Empresas0.zip             keep — the only candidate this file yields
       3. /public.php/webdav/2026-09/                  skipped today — resourcetype/collection
       4. https://evil.example/public.php/webdav/Evil.zip
                                                       drop: host — an absolute foreign href.
                                                       `_nextcloud_public_file_url` uses only
                                                       urlsplit(href).path, so today this is
                                                       silently *re-homed* onto the configured
                                                       base rather than dropped, and nothing
                                                       logs it.
       5. file:///public.php/webdav/Local.zip          drop: scheme
       6. /public.php/webdav/2026-09/../../etc/passwd  keep, but contained: the filename must be
                                                       the bare name `passwd` and the produced
                                                       location must stay under the configured
                                                       base with no `..` segment. Today
                                                       `_nextcloud_public_file_url` re-attaches
                                                       the traversal verbatim.
-->
